card.statement:
The following relations hold in $\K_q(\bar x,\bar y)^{S_n}$:

\begin{align}
[t_i,t_j]&=0,\qquad\forall i,j\in\iv{1}{n},\\
[e_k,e_l]&=0,\qquad\forall k,l\in\iv{0}{n},\\
t_je_k - q^{\delta_{j+k>n}}e_kt_j &
=(q-1)\sum_{i\in\Z\setminus I(n-(j+k))}
(-1)^{i+\delta_{i<0}} e_{k+i} t_{j+i},
\end{align}

for all $ j\in\iv{1}{n}$ and $k\in\iv{0}{n}$, where $\delta_P$ is the Kronecker delta <<ref:eq:kronecker>> and for all $k\in\Z$ we put

\begin{equation}
I(k):=\iv{\min(0,k+1)}{\max(0,k)}=
\begin{cases}
\iv{0}{k},&k\ge 0,\\
\iv{k+1}{0},&k<0,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

and, by convention, $t_j=0$ if $j\notin\iv{1}{n}$ and $e_k=0$ if $k\notin\iv{0}{n}$.
